WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.267
President Biden and House Speaker

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.836
Kevin McCarthy have reached a deal

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.004
to raise the debt limit.

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.372
And now they are racing

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:06.573
to convince lawmakers

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.041
on both sides of the aisle

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:09.209
to back the plan.

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:10.443
The House is set to vote on the deal

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:13.046
just two days from now.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:15.715
What do you say to members

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:16.583
of your own party

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:17.484
who say you need

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:19.686
to make concessions in this deal?

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:20.253
Well, find

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:21.388
I didn't think you're going

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:22.589
to get a majority of Republicans

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:23.523
voting for this bill.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.591
This is a good bill

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:25.825
for the American public.

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:27.360
The president agreed with this bill.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.194
So I think there's going to be

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:28.928
a lot of Democrats

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:30.563
are going to vote for two.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.799
And the House Progressive Caucus already

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.434
speaking out against new work

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:35.468
requirements in the deal

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:36.903
for food stamp recipients.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:41.041
It is

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:42.108
really unfortunate

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:42.809
that the president

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.177
opened the door to this.

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:46.679
And while at the end of the day,

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.782
perhaps this will

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:50.050
because of the exemptions,

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.618
perhaps it will be okay.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:52.685
I can't commit to that.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:55.155
I really don't know.

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.123
And the conservative House Freedom

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.024
Caucus also

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:59.526
pushing back against the deal, saying

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:01.761
it does not cut enough spending.

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:02.695
Some key members

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.864
tweeted, no Republican capitulation

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:06.733
and hold the line.

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:07.700
As for the debt ceiling,

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.435
the latest warning

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.603
from Treasury Secretary Janet Yellen

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:11.771
estimates that the government

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:12.772
could run out of money

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:13.273
to pay

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:14.507
all of its debts on time,

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.810
the so-called X date on June 5th.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.378
One week from today,

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:20.480
CNN chief correspondent Manu Raju

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.115
live for us on Capitol Hill. So, Manu.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:22.949
For those of us

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:24.384
just waking up on a Monday morning

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:25.351
who may not have been following

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.486
the Saturday and Sunday

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:28.321
break, the deal for us

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:30.123
Yeah, look, this was a hard

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.025
fought negotiation and negotiation

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:32.892
that the White House didn't

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:34.094
want to have to begin with.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.628
Remember President Biden

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:37.163
for about three months,

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:38.131
more than three months,

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.632
just refused to sit down

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:40.500
with Kevin McCarthy

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.869
because he demanded the debt ceiling

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.037
be increased,

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:47.040
$31.4 trillion debt ceiling be increased

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:48.575
without any conditions,

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:50.043
without any spending cuts.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.778
Warning that averting

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:52.278
trying to do

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:55.181
so would avert a fiscal disaster here.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:55.682
But Kevin

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.016
McCarthy had a different approach.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:57.750
He demanded

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.485
spending cuts,

00:01:58.485 --> 00:01:59.752
a whole slew of conditions.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:00.453
Ultimately,

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.455
the White House was forced to negotiate

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:04.591
and make a range of concessions

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.826
that is angering both sides of the aisle.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:07.994
Some liberals upset

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:09.496
and also some conservatives upset

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:10.930
with the deal that McCarthy cut.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:11.998
Now, a little bit about the deal,

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.032
two year

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:14.701
suspension of the debt limit

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:15.869
essentially would expire

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:16.803
in January of 20.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:19.506
25 That is got some concern on the right

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:20.073
they believe that

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.441
it should have only been one year

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:22.175
for allowing them

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:23.743
preventing them from fighting this again

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.111
next year in an election year

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:25.979
also to ensure

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:27.881
that veterans and medical care

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:30.350
is not impacted by the spending cuts

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.751
that would have happened across the board

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:32.852
on domestic programs.

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.921
There's essentially a

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.122
for defense programs

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.390
there's not a cut for defense

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.625
but that's caused some concerns

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.393
among defense hawks who believe that

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:41.127
that is not

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:42.395
they need to have more money

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:43.163
for the Pentagon.

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:44.464
So expect some pushback

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:45.598
from the right on that.

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:46.599
But that's also

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.034
it would expand work requirements

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.636
for food stamp recipients.

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:51.504
That has caused a lot of angst

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:52.605
among on the left.

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.274
And it has a whole host of other issues,

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:56.176
such as cutting IRS funding

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:57.243
that's caused some concern

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:58.278
among Democrats,

00:02:58.278 --> 00:03:00.213
as well as rescinding unspent Kobani

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:02.215
that actually had some bipartisan support

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:03.183
as part of this deal.

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:04.918
And one thing to watch that actually

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:05.485
could generate

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:07.287
some opposition from progressives

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:08.054
is that it

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:10.023
would actually expedite construction

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.224
of a pipeline

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:13.393
in West Virginia, a big priority

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:15.528
for West Virginia Senator Joe Manchin.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:15.962
But something

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:17.797
that progressives in particular

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:18.865
were upset about.

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:20.233
Now, what the White House has been trying

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:21.067
to tell Democrats

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.202
what they did last night

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:23.970
in all these two briefings

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.471
with the House and Senate Democrats

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.440
was they could have been a lot worse.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.274
One of the things that

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:29.209
did not make it in

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:30.877
this bill was to impose

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:32.111
new work requirements

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:34.547
for recipients of the Medicaid health

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:35.181
insurance program

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:37.217
because it's a low income health

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.484
care program.

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.420
Republicans had pushed for new work

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.788
requirements for those recipients

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:43.189
that did not get in the bill.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:44.123
They also argued

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:45.558
a whole host of other issues,

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:46.526
such as the president's

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:47.460
signature inflation

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.429
reduction Act, was not cut

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:51.497
as Republicans had pushed for,

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:52.932
which is what they're trying to convince

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:53.399
Democrats.

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:54.534
This is the best

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:55.501
we can get,

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.703
even as a lot of folks

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:57.704
on the right saying

00:03:57.704 --> 00:03:59.706
those cuts should have been imposed

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:01.341
and McCarthy should have demanded more

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:02.942
and should not have given the president.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:03.643
And as long

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:04.210
the debt

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:05.311
limits expansion

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.347
as it's in this current deal,

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.915
causing a lot of angst

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.450
on both wings of the party

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.552
as they try to get this to Congress,

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:13.086
a lot of angst,

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:14.854
a lot of unpredictability moneywise you.

00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:15.688
Thank you.

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:17.190
We shall see. Yes, we will.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:17.724
I want to bring in

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:19.225
now CNN economics commentator

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:19.826
and Washington Post

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:21.594
opinion columnist Catherine Rampell

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:22.829
and former Democratic congressman

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:24.264
from New York, Max Rose, who's also,

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:25.298
of course, a veteran of the war

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:26.432
in Afghanistan.

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:27.333
He received a Purple Heart,

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:28.434
among other honors.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.403
Nice to see you both this morning.

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:31.170
I'm going to start with you.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.505
When we look at what's happening here

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:34.607
and I think,
you know, as Manu laid out for us,

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.075
we know there's a lot of skepticism.

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:36.843
There's a lot of angst

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:38.645
on both sides of the aisle here.

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:40.480
But we pressed people a lot

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.115
and we say, I need a yes or no answer,

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:44.050
as you know all too well.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:46.052
And Congresswoman Jayapal actually

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:48.087
gave Jake Tapper a one word answer

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:49.022
when he said,

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:49.856
does the president

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:50.890
basically need to be worried here?

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:51.691
And she said, yes,

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:53.559
you should be worried about progressives

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:55.261
if the White House messaging is, hey,

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:56.696
it could have been worse.

00:04:56.696 --> 00:04:57.630
Is that really enough

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:58.831
to convince progressives

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.600
it will be enough for it to pass?

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.534
It will not be enough

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.136
to convince progressives.

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.470
So you have this incredibly

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.740
fascinating dynamic right now where

00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:10.610
Kevin McCarthy and Joe Biden

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:11.311
and potentially

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.111
also the leader

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:13.379
of the Democratic caucus, Hakeem

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:15.248
Jeffries, will all be working in tandem

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:16.049
together

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:17.550
to pass this legislation,

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.552
of course, to avoid economic catastrophe,

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:22.322
but also because it is in their political

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:25.925
best interests now with this bill,

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:28.461
the administration has certainly cemented

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:30.663
the fact that it is absolutely,

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:31.597
resolutely committed

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:33.866
to bipartisanship and normalcy

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.068
And in the process,

00:05:35.068 --> 00:05:36.002
I actually think

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:37.036
that they have boxed

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.071
the Republican Party

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:40.540
into this really awful corner

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:41.441
where by now

00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:43.076
the Republican Party has to advocate

00:05:43.076 --> 00:05:44.243
for increased spending.

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:44.610
Of course,

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.679
because the debt ceiling will be raised

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:48.181
by trillions of dollars

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:50.183
and for increased social service

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:50.850
spending.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.052
Now, with an expansion of SNAP benefits,

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:55.722
for veterans as well as the homeless.

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:56.956
On the other hand,

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:58.658
the Republican Party can say

00:05:58.658 --> 00:05:59.792
the Democratic Party

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:01.627
did not get any of their priorities

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:04.030
in there and that, yes, is true as well.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.365
So it might be the sign

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:06.933
of a great negotiation

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.968
that nobody is happy right now,

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:09.602
but this will

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:11.070
certainly pass will pass

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.805
because of moderates

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:14.040
on both sides of the aisle.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.408
And they will largely do that

00:06:15.408 --> 00:06:17.410
because they do not want to be the reason

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.078
for economic calamity.

00:06:19.078 --> 00:06:19.412
Catherine,

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:20.747
let me bring you into the conversation,

00:06:20.747 --> 00:06:22.448
because there's been a lot of drama.

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:23.816
There's been a lot of noise.

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:25.251
And you say in a recent op ed

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:26.652
that there has already been

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:27.353
some harm done,

00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:29.155
even if we don't actually default.

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:29.956
Yes.

00:06:29.956 --> 00:06:32.392
Look, I look at this deal and say

00:06:32.425 --> 00:06:34.227
how is it any different than what

00:06:34.227 --> 00:06:34.560
we would have

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:35.528
reasonably expect

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:37.130
to get from the usual annual

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:38.398
appropriations process?

00:06:38.398 --> 00:06:40.666
It's really not that different

00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:43.536
given divided government Republicans

00:06:43.536 --> 00:06:46.272
didn't get the draconian cuts

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:47.140
that they asked for.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:47.573
They didn't get

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:48.808
the Medicaid work requirements.

00:06:48.808 --> 00:06:49.842
They didn't get some of the other things

00:06:49.842 --> 00:06:50.743
that I was worried about,

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:52.345
including basically

00:06:52.345 --> 00:06:54.380
undermining the entire regulatory state.

00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:57.049
They basically got flat spending,

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:57.884
which, again, is

00:06:57.884 --> 00:06:58.718
what I would have expected

00:06:58.718 --> 00:07:00.887
coming out of the appropriations process.

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:02.889
So the question is fine,

00:07:03.222 --> 00:07:04.824
but what was it all for?

00:07:04.824 --> 00:07:05.425
Right.

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:07.627
We've gone through all of this drama.

00:07:07.627 --> 00:07:08.461
We've gone through

00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:09.662
economic turmoil,

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:11.431
basically embarrassing ourselves

00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:12.532
on the world stage.

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:14.567
Biden having to cut his Asia trip short.

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:16.335
The G-7 kind of being overshadowed

00:07:16.335 --> 00:07:17.904
by all of this.

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:19.005
Not to mention probably

00:07:19.005 --> 00:07:20.373
higher borrowing costs

00:07:20.373 --> 00:07:22.708
as a result of some market stresses.

00:07:23.075 --> 00:07:25.244
And we ended up where we would have been

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:27.146
had this whole brinksmanship

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:28.815
episode never happened.

00:07:28.815 --> 00:07:31.250
So on the one hand, I'm glad

00:07:31.818 --> 00:07:33.653
that we knock on wood,

00:07:33.653 --> 00:07:34.620
you know, don't look like we're

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:37.223
about to have a financial apocalypse

00:07:37.223 --> 00:07:38.491
and we and that Republicans

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:39.992
didn't get all these other things in.

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:41.828
But like what was the point?

00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:43.796
We could have avoided all of this.

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:45.264
Catherine, you and I have talked about

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:47.800
in passing actually here at CNN, your

00:07:49.001 --> 00:07:50.503
how you feel about IRS reform.

00:07:50.503 --> 00:07:51.103
And I'm curious

00:07:51.103 --> 00:07:52.572
what you think about the concessions

00:07:52.572 --> 00:07:54.340
that looks like the IRS reform

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:56.242
will receive as part of this bill.

00:07:56.242 --> 00:07:58.044
I mean,
do you think it would be significant?

00:07:58.044 --> 00:07:59.312
Well,
they're cutting about

00:07:59.312 --> 00:08:00.880
a quarter of the funding

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:01.981
that was

00:08:02.014 --> 00:08:04.317
appropriated to the IRS last year,

00:08:04.317 --> 00:08:05.351
which I think is actually

00:08:05.351 --> 00:08:06.953
quite a bad thing.

00:08:06.953 --> 00:08:08.221
That money has a huge

00:08:08.221 --> 00:08:09.689
return on investment,

00:08:09.689 --> 00:08:11.591
both because it means better

00:08:11.591 --> 00:08:12.825
customer services

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:14.527
and taxpayers are happier

00:08:14.527 --> 00:08:16.429
and they're more voluntarily compliant.

00:08:16.429 --> 00:08:17.463
And it means that

00:08:17.463 --> 00:08:19.265
the IRS has the resources to go after

00:08:19.265 --> 00:08:21.467
wealthy tax cheats and corporations

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:22.935
So I don't think this was a good place

00:08:22.935 --> 00:08:23.369
to cut money.

00:08:23.369 --> 00:08:25.505
In fact, it will expand deficits.

00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:26.606
That said, you know,

00:08:26.606 --> 00:08:28.274
they did some kind of accounting gimmicks

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:29.108
where it doesn't look like

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:29.942
it's materially

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:31.544
going to affect the irises

00:08:32.612 --> 00:08:33.679
overall in the

00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:34.347
near term,

00:08:34.347 --> 00:08:35.815
it'll probably be more of a problem

00:08:35.815 --> 00:08:36.849
several years from now.

00:08:36.849 --> 00:08:39.986
But again, it's it's not making it easier

00:08:39.986 --> 00:08:41.521
for rich people to cheat on their taxes.

00:08:41.521 --> 00:08:43.189
Doesn't seem like the thing you would do

00:08:43.189 --> 00:08:44.023
if you really cared

00:08:44.023 --> 00:08:46.592
about getting deficits under control.

00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:47.026
Interesting, though,

00:08:47.026 --> 00:08:49.295
that will undoubtedly

00:08:49.295 --> 00:08:50.162
be put forth

00:08:50.162 --> 00:08:51.397
as a win for Republicans

00:08:51.397 --> 00:08:53.733
if they got some of that money back.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:56.269
How does this play to your point

00:08:56.269 --> 00:08:58.170
of, look,
if everybody's unhappy that

00:08:58.170 --> 00:08:58.471
I guess

00:08:58.471 --> 00:08:59.972
this is a good negotiation, right?

00:08:59.972 --> 00:09:02.108
Because nobody comes out the winner here,

00:09:02.108 --> 00:09:05.011
but how do you sell that to constituents?

00:09:05.044 --> 00:09:06.812
Well, there's a few major hurdles here

00:09:06.812 --> 00:09:07.380
just in terms

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:08.814
of selling it to legislators.

00:09:08.814 --> 00:09:09.582
First of all,

00:09:09.582 --> 00:09:12.385
Kevin McCarthy has to get over half

00:09:12.385 --> 00:09:14.387
of his own caucus to support this

00:09:14.554 --> 00:09:16.155
before it even gets to the floor.

00:09:16.155 --> 00:09:17.757
And they have not confirmed

00:09:17.757 --> 00:09:18.658
that they will do this.

00:09:18.658 --> 00:09:19.992
And that will be in process

00:09:19.992 --> 00:09:21.060
as it's known.

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.596
Behind the scenes is not fact-based.

00:09:23.896 --> 00:09:24.730
This at this point

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:26.732
will be deeply personal.

00:09:26.732 --> 00:09:27.867
The speaker wants this.

00:09:27.867 --> 00:09:28.801
The leader wants this.

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:30.136
The president wants this.

00:09:30.136 --> 00:09:31.470
Get in line

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.406
or else there's going to be consequences

00:09:33.406 --> 00:09:34.507
down the road that you can't take

00:09:34.507 --> 00:09:36.576
the politics out of politics.

00:09:36.576 --> 00:09:37.443
McCarthy is doing that

00:09:37.443 --> 00:09:38.611
because typically Republicans

00:09:38.611 --> 00:09:39.512
have done a very good job

00:09:39.512 --> 00:09:40.913
of getting their their caucus

00:09:40.913 --> 00:09:42.048
to fall in line.

00:09:42.048 --> 00:09:42.915
We are seeing something

00:09:42.915 --> 00:09:43.382
a little bit

00:09:43.382 --> 00:09:44.250
different here,

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:45.785
which certainly we saw play out

00:09:45.785 --> 00:09:47.820
when he was trying to get that gavel.

00:09:47.853 --> 00:09:48.421
Sure, sure.

00:09:48.421 --> 00:09:49.622
So he

00:09:49.622 --> 00:09:51.791
he will be fine at getting,

00:09:51.791 --> 00:09:53.426
I believe, more than 50%

00:09:53.426 --> 00:09:55.294
because you've already seen leaders

00:09:55.294 --> 00:09:57.096
in the moderate wing of that party.

00:09:57.096 --> 00:09:58.364
I wouldn't call the moderate.

00:09:58.364 --> 00:10:00.132
Let's just say less extreme

00:10:00.132 --> 00:10:02.101
wing of that party

00:10:02.101 --> 00:10:04.270
expressing their support for this.

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:06.272
With that being said, though,

00:10:06.272 --> 00:10:07.707
you know, the Democratic Party,

00:10:07.707 --> 00:10:09.842
I think that in that whipping process

00:10:09.842 --> 00:10:11.677
that we're seeing right now,

00:10:11.677 --> 00:10:14.013
what people will be upset by.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:14.614
Yes.

00:10:14.614 --> 00:10:15.615
Is the policy,

00:10:15.615 --> 00:10:16.749
but they're going to be more upset

00:10:16.749 --> 00:10:17.817
legislators to be more upset

00:10:17.817 --> 00:10:19.652
about two other things. One.

00:10:19.652 --> 00:10:21.420
Did we get anything out of this at all?

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:23.222
Our own priorities, Democratic

00:10:23.222 --> 00:10:24.657
core Democratic priorities.

00:10:24.657 --> 00:10:25.591
They got victories.

00:10:25.591 --> 00:10:27.093
What did we get?

00:10:27.093 --> 00:10:28.127
But secondly,

00:10:28.127 --> 00:10:29.662
I think that there will be certain

00:10:29.662 --> 00:10:32.665
angst around giving Kevin McCarthy a win.

00:10:32.999 --> 00:10:34.300
So they're going to want to see

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:35.201
the Republicans

00:10:35.201 --> 00:10:37.103
show momentum around the show

00:10:37.103 --> 00:10:38.838
that they can pass this themselves

00:10:38.838 --> 00:10:40.539
or come somewhat close to it

00:10:40.539 --> 00:10:41.440
before Democrats

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:44.043
start raising their hands and saying that

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:45.845
that they'll go about doing this.

00:10:45.845 --> 00:10:46.312
And of course,

00:10:46.312 --> 00:10:47.446
last to conclude,

00:10:47.446 --> 00:10:48.214
there's going to be folks,

00:10:48.214 --> 00:10:48.881
I want to turn this

00:10:48.881 --> 00:10:50.449
into a Christmas tree as well.

00:10:50.449 --> 00:10:51.550
I certainly wouldn't rule out

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:52.985
some people thinking about amendments.

00:10:52.985 --> 00:10:55.321
How can I get my little appropriation

00:10:55.321 --> 00:10:56.656
associated with that?

00:10:56.656 --> 00:10:57.723
You'll see a lot of that over

00:10:57.723 --> 00:10:58.924
the coming days. That shouldn't happen.

